---
// The interactive filter visualiser. The markup is plain HTML; the behaviour
// lives in src/scripts/visualiser, which runs the real compiled filter.
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Watch one observation pass through the filter',
    description: 'An interactive visualiser that runs the Fonn output filter in your browser. Pick a sample or paste your own output and watch each check decide what the model receives.',
    template: 'splash',
  }}
>
  <div class="viz-page not-content">
        <div class="viz-intro">
          <p class="lede">Every time the agent runs a Bash command, its output passes a row of checks before the model reads it. Fonn shortens the output only when every check passes. This page runs the same compiled filter code as the CLI, in your browser. Nothing is sent anywhere.</p>
        </div>

        <noscript>
          <p class="note viz-noscript">The visualiser needs JavaScript. The <a href="/start/overview/">docs page</a> shows a static before and after example, and <a href="#checks">the checks are described below</a>.</p>
        </noscript>

        <section id="visualiser" class="viz" aria-label="Filter visualiser" hidden>
          <div class="viz-controls">
            <div class="sample-field">
              <span class="viz-label" id="sample-label">Sample</span>
              <div class="theme-select sample-select">
                <button type="button" class="theme-select-button" id="sample-button" aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false" aria-labelledby="sample-label sample-current">
                  <span id="sample-current"></span>
                  <svg class="theme-select-chevron" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="12" height="12">
                    <path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
                  </svg>
                </button>
                <ul class="theme-select-menu" id="sample-list" role="listbox" aria-labelledby="sample-label" tabindex="-1" hidden></ul>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="viz-options">
              <fieldset class="segmented">
                <legend>Filter mode</legend>
                <div class="chip-row">
                  <label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="filter" checked><span>filter</span></label>
                  <label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="observe"><span>observe</span></label>
                  <label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="off"><span>off</span></label>
                </div>
              </fieldset>
              <fieldset class="segmented">
                <legend>Filter level</legend>
                <div class="chip-row" id="level-list">
                  <label><input type="radio" name="level" value="strict"><span>strict</span></label>
                  <label><input type="radio" name="level" value="standard" checked><span>standard</span></label>
                  <label><input type="radio" name="level" value="similar"><span>similar</span></label>
                </div>
              </fieldset>
              <button type="button" class="button" id="replay">Replay</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="viz-blurb" id="sample-blurb"></p>

          <div class="viz-grid">
            <article class="card card-input" aria-labelledby="input-title">
              <header class="card-head">
                <h2 id="input-title"><span class="step-no">1</span> Observation</h2>
                <span class="count" id="input-count"></span>
              </header>
              <label class="field-label" for="command">Bash command</label>
              <input id="command" class="field mono" type="text" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off">
              <label class="field-label" for="stdout">Output (stdout)</label>
              <textarea id="stdout" class="field mono" spellcheck="false" rows="16"></textarea>
              <p class="hint">Edit either field. The filter reruns as you type.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="card card-pipeline" aria-labelledby="pipe-title">
              <header class="card-head">
                <h2 id="pipe-title"><span class="step-no">2</span> Checks</h2>
                <span class="count" id="verdict"></span>
              </header>
              <ol class="pipeline" id="pipeline"></ol>
            </article>

            <article class="card card-output" aria-labelledby="out-title">
              <header class="card-head">
                <h2 id="out-title"><span class="step-no">3</span> Model receives</h2>
                <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="show-removed" checked> show removed</label>
              </header>
              <div class="meter" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="meter-row"><span>in</span><div class="bar"><i id="bar-in"></i></div><b id="chars-in"></b></div>
                <div class="meter-row"><span>out</span><div class="bar"><i id="bar-out"></i></div><b id="chars-out"></b></div>
              </div>
              <p class="sr-only" id="meter-text"></p>
              <div class="lines" id="lines" tabindex="0" aria-label="Delivered output with removed lines marked"></div>
              <p class="hint">Counts are characters in this observation. They are not tokens or dollars.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="card card-archive" aria-labelledby="archive-title" id="archive">
              <header class="card-head">
                <h2 id="archive-title"><span class="step-no">4</span> Archive and bounded recovery</h2>
                <span class="count" id="archive-id"></span>
              </header>
              <div id="archive-empty" class="archive-empty"><p>Nothing archived. The model received the original output, so there is nothing to recover.</p></div>
              <div id="archive-body" class="archive-body" hidden>
                <p>The full original is kept in the local state directory. The footer tells the agent how to read it back, one bounded slice at a time.</p>
                <div class="slice-controls">
                  <label>Offset <input type="number" id="offset" min="0" value="0" class="field mono"></label>
                  <label>Limit <input type="number" id="limit" min="1" max="20000" value="4000" class="field mono"></label>
                  <input type="range" id="offset-range" min="0" value="0" aria-label="Offset">
                </div>
                <pre class="cmd"><code id="recover-cmd"></code></pre>
                <p class="count" id="slice-info"></p>
                <pre class="output slice" tabindex="0"><code id="slice"></code></pre>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>
        <div class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" id="live"></div>

        <div class="viz-docs">
          <section id="checks" aria-labelledby="checks-title">
            <h2 id="checks-title">What each check means</h2>
            <dl class="checks">
              <div><dt>Filter mode</dt><dd><code>off</code> stops here. <code>observe</code> runs every check and archives the original, then delivers the full output anyway, so you can see what would change.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Plain shell text</dt><dd>The response must be ordinary stdout text. Images, interrupted commands, error responses and structured content pass through.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Not already filtered</dt><dd>Output that already carries a Fonn footer or duplicate note is never reduced twice.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>At least 2,000 characters</dt><dd>Short output has little to gain, so it is delivered as is.</dd></div>
              <div class="check-wide"><dt>Recognized format or repeated lines</dt><dd>Colour codes and carriage returns are refused first. A format adapter runs when the command is one direct call to PHPUnit, Pest, <code>artisan test</code>, PHPStan <code>analyse</code>, <code>tsc</code>, pytest, Jest or Vitest. <code>npm test</code> and friends try Jest and Vitest and the output shows the tool's own summary markers. Pipes, <code>;</code>, <code>&amp;&amp;</code>, quotes and <code>$</code> skip the adapters. Otherwise, at the standard level, the generic reduction looks for 3 or more identical adjacent lines. At the similar level it also looks for 4 or more lines that differ only in numbers or IDs. The strict level stops after the adapters.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Safe reduction exists</dt><dd>The adapter removes only exact progress rows or adjacent identical diagnostics. If nothing matches, nothing changes.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Saves at least 256 characters</dt><dd>The saving must outweigh the recovery footer that gets added.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Original archived</dt><dd>The full response is written to the local store before anything is shortened. If archiving fails, the original is delivered.</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </section>

          <section id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
            <h2 id="limits-title">What the filter never touches</h2>
            <ul class="features">
              <li>Model reasoning, conversation history and your instructions.</li>
              <li>Source files and anything on disk outside its own archive.</li>
              <li>Failures and warnings. Claude Code and Codex merge a command's stderr into the output, and those lines follow the same rules.</li>
              <li>Unknown formats and arbitrary MCP payloads, apart from runs of identical lines.</li>
              <li>Lines that mention errors, failures or warnings are never merged by similarity.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Native subagents inherit the same hooks, so their supported Bash observations go through these exact checks. Read the <a href="/reference/filtering/">filtering guide</a> or the <a href="https://github.com/nord-forge/fonn/blob/main/packages/core/src/filtering/adapters.ts">adapter source</a> for details.</p>
            <p><a class="inline-cta" href="/start/install/">Install Fonn</a></p>
          </section>
        </div>
  
  </div>
</StarlightPage>

<script>
  import '../scripts/visualiser/visualiser.js';
</script>
